/*
 * Explicit cast validation.
 *
 * CastExplicitValidation performs semantic validation of explicit casts between
 * values and types. It is responsible for:
 *
 *   - validating explicit cast operations,
 *   - handling enum-to-enum and enum-to-underlying-type casts,
 *   - delegating scalar and compound casts to specialized modules,
 *   - validating explicit casts to class pointer types,
 *   - producing rewritten values when explicit casts succeed,
 *   - propagating detailed diagnostics when explicit casts fail.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::operator::cast_::explicit
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/operator/cast_/explicit.yr
 * @Author(s):
